**Concept.** A four-drawer cabinet stands in a calm rest pose. The drawers slide out one after another from the top down, each on a spring with a slight overshoot. The most recently opened drawer carries the single bright stroke. At 5.8 s they close in reverse order, and the last frame matches the first, so the reel loops cleanly.

| Time | Action |
|---|---|
| 0–0.9 s | Rest. The top drawer handle is the one bright mark. |
| 0.9 / 2.0 / 3.1 / 4.2 s | Drawers 1, 2, 3 and 4 open in turn. |
| 5.8–6.6 s | They close, bottom drawer first. |
| 6.6–8 s | Rest, held. |

